      "text": "Given the equations:\n\\[\nab + bc + cd + da = 30\n\\]\n\\[\nb + d = 5\n\\]\n\nFirst, we can factor the left-hand side of the first equation:\n\\[\nab + bc + cd + da = b(a + c) + d(a + c)\n\\]\n\nThis can be rewritten as:\n\\[\nb(a + c) + d(a + c) = (b + d)(a + c)\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given value \\(b + d = 5\\) into the equation, we get:\n\\[\n(b + d)(a + c) = 5(a + c)\n\\]\n\nGiven that \\(ab + bc + cd + da = 30\\), we substitute this into the equation:\n\\[\n5(a + c) = 30\n\\]\n\nTo find \\(a + c\\), we solve for \\(a + c\\) by dividing both sides of the equation by 5:\n\\[\na + c = \\frac{30}{5} = 6\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(a + c\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]",
